// NpcScalingTable.h - the reference WPF tool's "scale bosses/tracked enemies
// to fit wherever they land" data, generated verbatim from its own
// Mod Files/NPC Scaling File/NPCScalingFile.txt and NPCParamsFile.txt (loaded
// at runtime by the reference tool; embedded here so the PS4 app doesn't need
// to ship or read them separately).
//
// kNpcParamsTable lists ~1170 "tracked" base NPCParamID values. kNpcScalingTable
// is a flat array where each tracked base value (verified present via a self-
// referential match: every kNpcParamsTable entry also appears somewhere in
// kNpcScalingTable) is immediately followed by ~31 pre-tuned "scaled variant"
// NPCParamIDs of that SAME creature, one per zone slot. ParamScalingForBosses
// (reference source, MainWindow.xaml.cs) finds where a tracked value sits in
// kNpcScalingTable, adds a per-zone offset (ScaleForZone below, the reference
// tool's own dreamScale/hemwickScale/etc. constants), and looks up the result -
// producing values that can look like nonsense (e.g. 900000006) but are real,
// intentional, hand-curated data the reference tool ships, not corruption.
